   "source": [
    "# Grid cell RNN: path integration in a 16 x 16 conceptual space\n",
    "\n",
    "Based on Cueva & Wei (2018). Self-contained: all the code is in the cells below (copied from `config.py`, `space.py`, `models.py`, `metrics.py`, `train_grid.py`). Run the cells top to bottom.\n",
    "\n",
    "| Setting | Value | Where |\n",
    "|---|---|---|\n",
    "| Arena | 16 x 16, coordinates -8..+8 | `SpaceConfig.arena_size` |\n",
    "| Trajectory | 100 velocity inputs; input *t* moves the agent from step *t* to *t+1* | `GridTrainConfig.seq_len` |\n",
    "| Input at t = 0 | start position (x0, y0), scaled to [-1, 1] | `generate_trajectories` |\n",
    "| Input every step | speed, cos(heading), sin(heading) | `SpaceConfig.input_mode` |\n",
    "| Output every step | (x, y) position after that step | `PathIntegratorRNN` |\n",
    "| Walls | near a wall, a heading pointing into it is reflected away, so velocities never leave the arena | `SpaceConfig.wall_margin` |\n",
    "| Stillness noise | 90% of speed inputs are 0 | `SpaceConfig.zero_speed_frac` |\n",
    "| RNN | vanilla leaky tanh RNN, 1 layer, 512 units, leak alpha = 0.1 | `RNNConfig` |\n",
    "| Loss | MSE + L1 firing-rate penalty (per unit, per time step) + L2 weight penalty (W_in, W_rec, W_out) | `compute_loss` |\n",
    "\n",
    "**Why the position is given only at t = 0:** if the network saw its true position every step, it could just add the velocity to it. Nothing would need to be integrated or remembered, and grid-like codes would have no reason to form. Giving only the start position makes it path-integrate, as in Cueva & Wei."
   ]
  },
